            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of abdominal pain in a patient with cystic fibrosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 19 year old man with cystic fibrosis (CF) who presented with atypical abdominal pain precipitated by pressing his ribs. This was subsequently discovered to be referred pain from an intercostal schwannoma. Surgical resection led to a resolution of his symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
